# ============================================
# What must NOT travel to the build machine.
#
# ⚠️ `.gitignore` IS NOT ENOUGH. eas-cli packs the working directory, and an
# ignored file is still a file on disk — the tarball grew from 33 MB to 39 MB
# carrying a build output the build machine is about to regenerate anyway.
#
# Worse than the size: shipping a stale `assets/shell/index.html` would let a
# build succeed with a UI built from somebody's laptop hours ago, instead of
# from the commit being built. `eas-build-post-install` rebuilds it from
# source; anything sent up would only ever be wrong or redundant.
# ============================================
assets/shell/

# Native build output — regenerated by prebuild/gradle on the machine.
android/build/
android/app/build/
android/.gradle/
ios/build/

# The same build output, at its Android path.
android/app/src/main/assets/shell/
